      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Horizon-scale imaging made black-hole structure an observable, opening a powerful new window on strong gravity. The result is both a major technical achievement and a lasting advance in astrophysics.",
        "attribution": "The proposed trio represents the theoretical case, the long-baseline interferometry foundation, and the effort that brought the global array to the horizon scale. Credit across the many participating observatories and teams needs careful examination.",
        "maturity": "The 2019 image and subsequent observations establish a durable result, with improvements in resolution and analysis continuing.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "How to apportion credit among the named leaders and the very large collaboration.",
          "How much the imaging itself tests gravity beyond confirming expected black-hole-scale structure."
        ]
      }
    },
